% A recursion that computes a new integer per round never reaches a fixed
% point; the target's limits must stop it in the optimized context and in
% the one whose rounds are deferred, and each must report the stop.
n(0).
n(Y) :- n(X), Y = X + 1.
pair(X, Y) :- n(X), n(Z), Y = X * 3 - Z.
n(X), X > 5?
pair(X, Y)?
